<h1 class="about-title order-title">
CONSTITUTION
</h1>

<hr class="order-rule">





<h3 class="about-subtitle">I — Purpose of the Order</h3>

<p class="about-text">
1. To investigate mysteries of philosophy, science, history, and consciousness.<br>
2. To preserve and transmit knowledge between generations.<br>
3. To serve as a collective of individuals dedicated to wisdom and discovery.<br> <br>
Organisation does not concern itself with temporary politics or worldly disputes.
</p>

<div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>


<h3 class="about-subtitle">II — Core Virtues</h3>

<p class="about-text">

<span class="accent">
<strong>Humility</strong><br><br>

<strong>Perseverance</strong><br><br>

<strong>Sharing</strong><br><br>

<strong>Gratitude</strong><br><br></span>

Heralds of the Lion swear to remain humble sages.<br>
These four virtues form the pillars of the Herald.<br>
For this reason, being a Herald must never be treated as an honor, although
it is one of the highest degree.
</p>

<div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>


